WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.540
Welcome.

2
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:08.360
This practice will move through posture, body, breath, sound, and a few moments of open awareness.

3
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.300
Nothing has to feel special.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.090
Choose a position you can change easily, and keep your eyes open whenever that feels more supportive.

5
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.050
You can pause or stop at any time.

6
00:00:33.064 --> 00:00:35.174
Begin by looking around.

7
00:00:36.874 --> 00:00:42.484
Notice three ordinary things in the room: perhaps a color, an edge, and a source of light.

8
00:00:44.184 --> 00:00:45.114
Hear one sound.

9
00:00:46.814 --> 00:00:48.854
Feel the surface beneath you.

10
00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:53.084
Let these simple facts confirm where you are.

11
00:01:06.851 --> 00:01:08.691
Arrange the body with enough support.

12
00:01:10.391 --> 00:01:13.911
If you are sitting, let the feet or legs find a stable place.

13
00:01:15.611 --> 00:01:18.621
If you are lying down, allow the surface to receive your weight.

14
00:01:20.321 --> 00:01:22.701
Let the hands rest without needing a formal shape.

15
00:01:41.058 --> 00:01:42.868
Notice the whole body at once.

16
00:01:44.568 --> 00:01:47.808
Not every detail, just the sense of a body taking up space.

17
00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:53.358
Feel where the body touches a surface and where it meets the air.

18
00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:14.324
Move attention slowly through a few regions.

19
00:02:16.024 --> 00:02:17.924
Begin with the feet and lower legs.

20
00:02:19.624 --> 00:02:23.454
Notice pressure, temperature, movement, or very little sensation.

21
00:02:25.154 --> 00:02:27.274
All of these are valid experiences.

22
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.520
Include the hips and the places that carry weight.

23
00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.440
Then notice the hands and arms.

24
00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.870
There is no need to relax them.

25
00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.530
Let them be known as they are.

26
00:03:27.476 --> 00:03:30.496
Bring attention to the shoulders, neck, and face.

27
00:03:32.196 --> 00:03:34.846
Notice the jaw and the space around the eyes.

28
00:03:36.546 --> 00:03:41.076
If a small adjustment is needed, make it slowly and feel the new position settle.

29
00:04:04.022 --> 00:04:05.182
Now find the breath.

30
00:04:06.882 --> 00:04:09.572
Do not take a demonstration breath.

31
00:04:11.272 --> 00:04:19.082
Wait for the next inhale to arrive and notice where it can be felt most clearly: at the nose, in the chest, or around the belly.

32
00:04:37.438 --> 00:04:40.048
Stay for one full inhale and one full exhale.

33
00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:44.998
Let the breath choose its own depth and timing.

34
00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:15.363
Attention may move into a thought or sound.

35
00:05:17.063 --> 00:05:21.593
When you notice, feel one point of contact and return to the breath that is happening now.

36
00:05:23.293 --> 00:05:28.143
Wandering is not a detour from the practice; noticing it is part of the practice.

37
00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:03.267
For a few breaths, silently use the words in and out if they help.

38
00:06:04.967 --> 00:06:06.737
Let the words remain quiet and simple.

39
00:06:08.437 --> 00:06:10.517
If they get in the way, release them.

40
00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:49.980
Now let the breath move into the background and listen.

41
00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.650
Receive the closest sound you can hear.

42
00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.320
Then receive a more distant sound.

43
00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.700
You do not need to name either one.

44
00:07:28.235 --> 00:07:30.445
Notice how sounds arrive without being invited.

45
00:07:32.145 --> 00:07:34.665
They change, overlap, and end.

46
00:07:36.365 --> 00:07:43.025
If a sound is unpleasant, you can keep some attention on the support beneath the body while acknowledging that the sound is present.

47
00:08:15.149 --> 00:08:17.369
Widen listening in every direction.

48
00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:20.609
Let the room have its full soundscape.

49
00:08:22.309 --> 00:08:26.959
The breath continues, the body remains supported, and hearing opens around both.

50
00:09:08.261 --> 00:09:11.071
We will now allow awareness to become a little wider.

51
00:09:12.771 --> 00:09:16.961
Include body sensations, breath, sound, and thoughts in one field.

52
00:09:18.661 --> 00:09:20.631
You do not need to keep track of everything.

53
00:09:22.331 --> 00:09:24.631
Notice only what becomes clear by itself.

54
00:10:01.344 --> 00:10:03.194
A sensation may come forward.

55
00:10:04.894 --> 00:10:05.974
Then a sound.

56
00:10:07.674 --> 00:10:09.404
Then a thought or image.

57
00:10:11.104 --> 00:10:14.564
Each can be present for a moment and move back.

58
00:10:16.264 --> 00:10:22.844
If anything feels too strong, open your eyes, look around, and return to the feet or another steady contact.

59
00:11:08.736 --> 00:11:12.056
Notice whether anything in experience stays completely still.

60
00:11:13.756 --> 00:11:14.786
A breath turns.

61
00:11:16.486 --> 00:11:17.766
A sound changes.

62
00:11:19.466 --> 00:11:20.196
Pressure shifts.

63
00:11:21.896 --> 00:11:23.446
A thought loses its place.

64
00:11:25.146 --> 00:11:28.386
You do not have to produce change; you can let change reveal itself.

65
00:12:09.688 --> 00:12:11.778
Return to one anchor for a quieter minute.

66
00:12:13.478 --> 00:12:17.168
Choose the breath, the hands, the feet, or sound.

67
00:12:18.868 --> 00:12:23.968
Each time attention wanders, recognize the moment and begin again with the chosen anchor.

68
00:13:19.038 --> 00:13:20.058
Release the anchor.

69
00:13:21.758 --> 00:13:25.798
Feel the whole body again, from the points of support to the top of the head.

70
00:13:27.498 --> 00:13:29.888
Include the room and the air around you.

71
00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:55.023
Notice how you are meeting this final part.

72
00:13:56.723 --> 00:14:02.343
Perhaps calm is present, perhaps restlessness, tiredness, or no obvious change.

73
00:14:04.043 --> 00:14:06.353
The practice does not require a particular result.

74
00:14:08.053 --> 00:14:10.323
Showing up and noticing are enough.

75
00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.240
Let the eyes focus clearly.

76
00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:34.540
Listen for one close and one distant sound.

77
00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:39.820
Move the fingers and toes, or make another small movement that feels right.

78
00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.540
Take your time changing position.

79
00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:51.570
You have practiced several ways of returning: through the ground, the body, the breath, and sound.

80
00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:55.090
You do not need to remember all of them.

81
00:14:56.790 --> 00:15:00.000
Choose one simple doorway the next time you want to arrive.
